<!--
  ============================================================================
  Jawa_MiningDisabled.xml                    StarWarsRaces · authored 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  JAWA_CANNOT_DIG_GENE_1. The owner's ruling, verbatim: "they should not be able
  to mine ore, though some other races still can. And the mining laser should be
  able to do this very well."

  WHY A GENE AND NOT A ScenPart
  =============================
  A `Rule_DisallowDesignator_Mine` is COLONY-WIDE, so a recruited Ugnaught could
  not mine either — and the owner said "some other races still can". A gene is
  per-pawn, which delivers that exactly, and it reaches ENEMY Jawa factions as
  well, which nothing else buys.

  WHY `disabledWorkTags` HERE AND AN APTITUDE FOR FARMING
  ======================================================
  Not an inconsistency — the WorkTags enum is simply not symmetrical. `PlantWork`
  is the ONLY plant tag and it covers `PlantCutting` as well as `Growing`, so
  disabling it would also stop a Jawa harvesting and CHOPPING TREES. No wood, on
  a scavenger clan. So farming took the soft lever (`AptitudeTerrible_Plants`,
  on the xenotype). `Mining` covers the `Mining` work type and nothing else, so
  the hard lever is clean here and it is what the owner asked for.

  🔑 AND THE DEEP DRILL GOES WITH IT, DELIBERATELY. Vanilla's `Drill` WorkGiver
  is `workType Mining`, so this gene stops a Jawa operating one. The owner
  accepted that asymmetry explicitly: the laser works, the drill beside it does
  not. ⛔ Do not "fix" it by patching vanilla's Drill WorkGiver — that would
  re-type the job for every faction in the game.

  ⚠️ THE TURRET STILL WORKS BECAUSE IT IS NO LONGER A MINING JOB.
  `DRILLTURRET_IS_A_SHOOTING_JOB_1` (fe0064c) moved `OperateDrillTurret` to
  `workType Hunting`. Hunting's workTags include `Violent`, so this design also
  depends on Jawa being CAPABLE of violent work. Measured 2026-08-22: no other
  gene on `MandrakeJawa` disables any work tag. If one is ever added, the turret
  silently stops being operable and nothing will say so.

  SHAPE
  =====
  Modelled on Biotech's `ViolenceDisabled`, which is the only shipped gene of
  this exact form — `disabledWorkTags Violent`, `biostatMet 3`, `biostatCpx 1`.
  ⛔ NO NEW ART. `iconPath` is the one Biotech's own `AptitudeTerrible_Mining`
  uses, which is proof it resolves. It is not a loose PNG on disk and it does
  not need to be.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GeneDef>
    <defName>RimMandrake_Jawa_MiningDisabled</defName>
    <label>cannot dig</label>
    <labelShortAdj>non-digging</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers of this gene cannot mine. The hands are wrong for it — narrow, soft-knuckled, built for stripping a wreck rather than breaking a seam — and the flinch response that keeps a Jawa alive in a collapsing hull makes standing under unsupported rock unbearable. They will not swing a pick and they will not stand at a deep drill.\n\nThis is not squeamishness about ore. A Jawa will happily run a machine that does the digging for it, and considers that the correct arrangement.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Skills/Mining/Terrible</iconPath>
    <displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
    <displayOrderInCategory>1790</displayOrderInCategory>
    <biostatMet>3</biostatMet>
    <biostatCpx>1</biostatCpx>
    <disabledWorkTags>Mining</disabledWorkTags>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
